<title>USA: Some US cash DAP, ammonia prices fall on supply.</title>
<headline>Some US cash DAP, ammonia prices fall on supply.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some U.S. cash diammonium phosphate (DAP) values and ammonia prices were lower Wednesday on continued supply pressure, cash dealers said.</p>
<p>Oversupply in world markets has kept ammonia and urea prices from rising, and that pressure has left many U.S. dealers reluctant to take on inventory, cash sources said.</p>
<p>			     Dlrs/short ton	 Chg from Monday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	  174-176		     unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf    185-187		     dn 1</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		220		     dn 5</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
